<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Lamjung</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.) · capital Lamjung</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A hill kingdom of central Nepal from whose ruling house the Shah kings of Gorkha, and thus of Nepal, descended.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lamjung emerged around 1500 in the hills of the Marsyangdi valley, ruled by a dynasty that claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> descent. Its kings gained prominence among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaubise-rajya">Chaubise Rajya</a>, the twenty-four principalities of central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Nepal</a>. In 1559 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drabya-shah">Drabya Shah</a>, a younger son of the Lamjung ruler, founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gorkha-kingdom">Gorkha Kingdom</a> to the east.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lamjung was a small agricultural state of terraced fields with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurung">Gurung</a> population and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> ruling family. Its kings competed with their <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gorkha-kingdom">Gorkha</a> kinsmen for influence and allied at times with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tanahun">Kingdom of Tanahun</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-palpa">Kingdom of Palpa</a> against Gorkha expansion. Few detailed records survive.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah's</a> conquests, Lamjung was annexed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a> in 1782. It is now Lamjung district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:5.61%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1782 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lamjung</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nepali, Gurung</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nepal">Nepal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lamjung</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lamjung" aria-label="Kingdom of Lamjung on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6865 1145 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Lamjung lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7239 1418h0M7218 1408h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7185 1401h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7185 1401h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Nepal. <a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lamjung">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

